{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "AKR Knowledge Reminder",
  "description": "Reminds the agent about the AKR knowledge repository on every prompt, triggering a fetch for relevant prior knowledge before responding.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "promptSubmit"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You have access to three tiers of intelligence for this codebase. Evaluate the user's request and determine which tiers are needed. Lean towards using all three — when in doubt, fetch. The ONLY time you should skip is for trivial, self-contained requests that clearly need no context (e.g. 'format this line', 'add a comma here', 'what time is it').\n\nComplete these steps in order before responding:\n1. Read `.kiro/steering/agent-knowledge.md` into context for full AKR usage rules and command reference.\n2. Read `.kiro/steering/codebase-intelligence.md` into context for genero-tools queries and combined workflow patterns.\n3. Run `akr-fetch --query \"<brief summary of the user's request>\"` to retrieve relevant prior knowledge.\n4. If the task involves modifying or understanding specific functions, run `bash $GENERO_TOOLS_PATH find-function-resolved <name>` and `bash $GENERO_TOOLS_PATH find-function-dependents <name>` for structural context.\n5. If the task involves understanding a module's business logic, data flows, integrations, or batch processes, read the relevant system documentation file using `$ELECTRA_DOCUMENTATION` (e.g. `cat $ELECTRA_DOCUMENTATION/01-module-summaries/<module>.md`). Consult `.kiro/steering/system-documentation.md` for which file to read based on the area you're working in.\n\nThe three tiers provide complementary information:\n- **genero-tools** (Tier 1): Codebase structure — function signatures, call graphs, schema, modules\n- **AKR** (Tier 2): Experiential context — patterns, bugs, decisions, gotchas from prior sessions\n- **System Documentation** (Tier 3): Business logic and module detail — what the system does and why, data flows, integrations, process inventories. Accessed via `$ELECTRA_DOCUMENTATION`.\n\nAlso, if during the interaction you discover something worth remembering (bug fix patterns, architectural decisions, code patterns, dependency insights), use `akr-commit` to persist it. The steering files have the full command reference.\n\nDo not ask the user for permission to run these steps. Execute them silently."
  }
}